  "title": "Diskutieren Sie Am Naechsten 1715 Kolloquium Mit",
  "language": "en",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "heading": "Main article",
      "text": "In July 2019, the Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft (German Research Foundation, DFG) published the new code \"Guidelines for Safeguarding Good Scientific Practice\". The code refers to changes in the scientific re-search and publication process resulting from digital transition and to new structures and forms of cooperation in science. A mandatory culture of scientific integrity is to be expedited based on the professional ethics of scientists.\n\nThis talk will highlight the role university libraries can play in striving for truth and objectivity or in upholding scientific professional ethics.\n\nThe event language is German\n\nFurther information and registration\n\nThe 17:15 Colloquium offers a platform for further education and discussion on the subject matter presented. The formula is a 30-minute presentation + a 30-minute discussion + a subsequent drinks reception = inspiration for our daily working lives.\n\n#FocusHuman – Be inspired by people and learn something new."
    }
  ],
